<title>USA: Conrail, CSX &quot;pleased&quot; with ruling.</title>
<headline>Conrail, CSX &quot;pleased&quot; with ruling.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>CSX Corp and Conrail Inc said on Wednesday they were pleased with a court ruling that allows a shareholder vote for the $9.2 billion merger of the two railroads to proceed.</p>
<p>&quot;We are pleased that the U.S. Court of Appeals has refused to enjoin the Conrail shareholder meeting set for Friday, January 17,&quot; the companies said in a joint statement.</p>
<p>The District Court decision rejected Norfolk Southern Corp's motion to invalidate the exclusivity period and block the shareholder vote scheduled for January 17.</p>
<p>Norfolk Southern, which also aims to takeover Conrail, requested that the courts block the meeting, claiming that the exclusivity provision could coerce Conrail holders into accepting the CSX offer.</p>
</text>
